  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Aggarwal vs The State Of Maharashtra on 16 October, 2025 Author: Dipankar Datta Bench: Dipankar Datta In The Supreme Court Of India Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Appeal No. /2025 [Arising out of Slp (Criminal) No.2339/2025] Anil Aggarwal & Ors. Appellants Versus The State Of Maharashtra Respondents With Criminal Appeal No. /2025 [Arising out of Slp (Criminal) No.4279/2025] Order",
    "facts": "The record reveals that after receiving the analysis report, the Local (Health) Authority sent the report to the Food Inspector, Latur, for further action. The complaint was filed on 11.05.2O07. The record and proceeding of the trial Court, particularly the roznama shows that on 15.05.20O7, the Local Health Officer Intimated the applicants under Section the court on 27.10.2009, and Applicants No.1 Anil Agrawal and No.2 Siddhant Khosla appeared in the Court on 22.03.2010 Date: 2025.10.17 16:43:36 IST",
    "arguments": "To the extent relevant, the same reads as follows:- 13. Report of Public analyst.2 [(1) The public analyst shall deliver, in such form as may be prescribed, a report to the Local (Health) Authority of the result of the analysis of any article of food submitted to him for analysis. (2) On receipt of the report of the result of the analysis under sub- section (1) to the effect that the article of food is adulterated, the Local (Health) Authority shall, after the institution of prosecution against the person from whom the sample of the article of food was taken and the person, if any, whose name, address and other particulars have been disclosed under section 14A, forward, in such manner as may be prescribed, a copy of the report of the result of the analysis to such person or persons, as the case may be, informing such person or persons that if it is so desired, either or both of them may make an application to the court within a period of ten days from the date of receipt of the copy of the report to get the sample of the article of food kept by the Local (Health) Authority analysed by the Central Food Laboratory.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "To the extent relevant, the same reads as follows:- 13. Report of Public analyst.2 [(1) The public analyst shall deliver, in such form as may be prescribed, a report to the Local (Health) Authority of the result of the analysis of any article of food submitted to him for analysis. (2) On receipt of the report of the result of the analysis under sub- section (1) to the effect that the article of food is adulterated, the Local (Health) Authority shall, after the institution of prosecution against the person from whom the sample of the article of food was taken and the person, if any, whose name, address and other particulars have been disclosed under section 14A, forward, in such manner as may be prescribed, a copy of the report of the result of the analysis to such person or persons, as the case may be, informing such person or persons that if it is so desired, either or both of them may make an application to the court within a period of ten days from the date of receipt of the copy of the report to get the sample of the article of food kept by the Local (Health) Authority analysed by the Central Food Laboratory."
  },
